# An allowlist, not a denylist: everything is excluded, and what the image is built from is let
# back in by name.
#
# A denylist is wrong by omission. It lists what exists on the day it is written, and the next file
# created at the root with a credential in it travels to the daemon without anyone having decided
# that. Here a new file has to be named below to be part of a build at all.
#
# It is also what makes this repository buildable in the first place: `.venv/` holds tens of
# thousands of small files inside a cloud-synced folder, and a denylist that forgot one entry would
# upload all of them as build context.

*

# What the build actually reads.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src
!alembic.ini
!migrations

# Not here as documentation. `pyproject.toml` declares `readme = "README.md"`, so hatchling refuses
# to build the wheel without it, and the failure surfaces from inside the build backend with no
# mention of this file.
!README.md

# Re-excluded after the two directories above are let in. A `__pycache__` written by a run on the
# host was compiled by the host's interpreter and has no business being copied into the image.
**/__pycache__
